From: Topeet <support@topeet.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] v4l2: Accept contiguous formats on multiplanar queues

The RK3588 HDMI RX uses the V4L2 multiplanar API while storing NV24's Y
and UV component planes in one contiguous memory plane. The driver
therefore correctly changes num_planes from the two GstVideoInfo
component planes to one V4L2 memory plane.

gst_v4l2_object_save_format() already supports this layout and
extrapolates the component offsets and strides from the single memory
plane. Allow that path to run when TRY_FMT or S_FMT returns one plane,
while continuing to reject all other unexpected plane-count changes.

Signed-off-by: Topeet <support@topeet.com>
---
 sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
@@ -3934,8 +3934,14 @@ gst_v4l2_object_set_format_full (GstV4l2Object * v4l2object, GstCaps * caps,
     align.padding_right = format.fmt.pix.width - width;
   }
 
-  if (is_mplane && format.fmt.pix_mp.num_planes != n_v4l_planes)
-    goto invalid_planes;
+  if (is_mplane && format.fmt.pix_mp.num_planes != n_v4l_planes) {
+    /* Component planes may share one contiguous V4L2 memory plane. */
+    if (format.fmt.pix_mp.num_planes != 1)
+      goto invalid_planes;
+    GST_INFO_OBJECT (v4l2object->dbg_obj,
+        "using one contiguous memory plane for %d component planes",
+        n_v4l_planes);
+  }
 
   /* used to check colorimetry and interlace mode fields presence */
   s = gst_caps_get_structure (caps, 0);
